al expansion of $(1+x)^{5}$ in ascending powers of $x$ to approximate $(0.94)^{5}.$ Give your answer to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when $n$ is a positive integer, \n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{1}{2!}n(n-1){x}^{2}+⋯+{x}^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1+x)}^{5} & =1+5x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot {x}^{2}+⋯+{x}^{5} \\\\  & =1+5x+10{x}^{2}+⋯+{x}^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for small $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{(1+x)}^{5}≈1+5x+10{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=-0.06$ into the above approximation of $(1+x)^{5}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0.94)^{6} & =(1+(-0.06))^{5} \\\\  & ≈1+5(-0.06)+10(-0.06)^{2} \\\\  & =1-5(0.06)+10(0.003\\,6) \\\\  & =1-0.3+0.036 \\\\  & =0.736,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto three decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134609/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e430ab-a814-5613-a45d-d8cdd3c14a0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134609"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-178291/selection/9b4a563ab877bc2aeae6b60e4fdb76c460d9e893cfc7913dc157c71b70e522e0" :answer/id #uuid "d7059860-768c-52ee-9600-97c54d3db95b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.315\\,84" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-178291/selection/7543d035abe0afe7b93354bb8359da6b18ff482b6d5e6490e910cb585f632af3" :answer/id #uuid "bde8833b-57d3-59da-b0a1-b93266680f3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.751\\,36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-178291/selection/a6065ea486976dbe8b031a13dd96987c5a6e2eef670942d973b9a5c445f91a47" :answer/id #uuid "962ffc73-4f0c-5c52-9f37-209eb2019402" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.751\\,47" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-178291/selection/4e74fd3b11a5784f4cc8f5e5ded5e47720a9f3f0d3dba7c6dd27f60f3e2f01ef" :answer/id #uuid "51bcb748-4216-5cfc-827f-12f0db8611fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.753\\,60" :db/ensure 